277
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:51,960
What is all this?

278
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:55,000
These figures are almost five, now ten times higher!

279
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:57,040
He's got more skills, too!

280
00:13:57,780 --> 00:14:00,340
Wait, there wasn't enough time for that to happen.

281
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:05,100
So then, he must have started using Fake Out after his first round of training.

282
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:09,080
He was already stronger than Chaos Machina from the get-go.

283
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:12,160
He was just grinding this whole time!

284
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:14,000
This guy is unhinged!

285
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,160
I mean, he's a complete and utter nut job!

286
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:20,280
Guess you're tougher than I expected!

287
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,200
Whatever!

288
00:14:24,140 --> 00:14:27,480
I'll summon all my magic into my fist using this ability!

289
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:29,160
The demonic and reach!

290
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:32,840
Turning you and this whole pathetic little town into...

291
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:35,000
Where'd you go?

292
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,940
When did you learn the flight skill?

293
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,180
How is that even possible?

294
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:44,460
She's one of the four heavenly kings.

295
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:45,680
Very powerful.

296
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:47,600
But she's careful, too.

297
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:50,760
She would have defeated any normal hero by this point.

298
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:55,000
However, she picked the wrong one this time.

299
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:57,240
Because now, this hero?

300
00:14:57,240 --> 00:15:01,560
Not the magic sword technique!

301
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:03,720
Isn't that an upper-tier skill?

302
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:05,260
It is.

303
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:07,540
It's called Phoenix Drive.

304
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:23,680
Oh, yeah.

305
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:27,320
This hero is unbelievably cautious.

306
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:42,120
What are you doing?

307
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:44,020
Don't make me get the hose.

308
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:44,920
I'm celebrating!

309
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:47,280
I thought we were done for back there!

310
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:48,800
Man, oh man.

311
00:15:49,140 --> 00:15:50,660
He smells good enough to eat.

312
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,060
Get off!

313
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:53,380
Give me a disease!

314
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:55,260
I am not gonna get you sick!

315
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:56,980
Come on, just let me have this!

316
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,460
I swear I'm perfectly healthy!

317
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:04,340
Honestly, though, I'm a little upset with you now.

318
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:06,740
Why have you been hiding your fake-out skill?

319
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:11,780
I figured if you had the ability to scan me, then any enemies might be able to do the same.

320
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:14,520
So I made sure to gain that skill before any others.

321
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:16,440
So you had it from the start?

322
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:19,460
I get keeping your true level away from baddies.

323
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:22,040
But don't you think you could have at least told me?

324
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:25,120
I mean, I am your partner after all, right?

325
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:28,700
Even if you kept your big mouth shut, there could be a brain monster.

326
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:31,040
One peek into your head and we'd be screwed.

327
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:31,880
Oh no!

328
00:16:31,940 --> 00:16:32,800
A brain monster!

329
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:34,460
That sounds really scary!

330
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:36,500
But I know that you would protect me!

331
00:16:36,740 --> 00:16:39,720
You're supposed to be a goddess, aren't you immortal?

332
00:16:40,140 --> 00:16:41,240
You don't need protection.

333
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:42,780
Not the point!

334
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:45,080
Cut it out, or I'll cut you.

335
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:46,580
Go right ahead!

336
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:47,760
Tear me to pieces!

337
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:48,600
Hey.

338
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:49,480
Huh?

339
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:50,260
Me?

340
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:52,580
Hey there, Mr. Hero.

341
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:54,960
We're so glad you saved our town.

342
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:56,800
I can't believe you beat that beast.

343
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:58,340
You have our eternal thanks.

344
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:00,320
He's got the face of a noble man.

345
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:02,440
Yes, and he's so tall and handsome, too.

346
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:05,060
Hello, I'm Jamie, and I run the fruit stand.

347
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:07,280
Please, go and help yourself.

348
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:08,860
Oh, thank you, Jamie.

349
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:10,280
Greetings!

350
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:11,720
I am the mayor of Eduna.

351
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:16,240
It would be my absolute pleasure to throw a banquet in your honor, so please join me at

352
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:16,860
my manor.

353
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:19,180
A welcoming party sure does sound nice.

354
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:19,880
Want to go?

355
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:22,520
No, I still have things to take care of, thank you very much.

356
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:25,280
But then he's heading straight to the next town.

357
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:26,740
How gallant.

358
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:28,960
No wonder I'm falling for him.

359
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:30,660
Uh, hey.

360
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:31,840
Whatcha doing?

361
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,160
Being safe.

362
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:35,980
Aren't those the charred remains of the mini bikini demon?

363
00:17:42,580 --> 00:17:43,720
Oh, no.

364
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:46,520
Casting Hell's Fire!

365
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:49,120
Not again!

366
00:17:51,220 --> 00:17:52,340
Hell's Fire!

367
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:53,520
Hell's Fire!

368
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:54,540
Hell's Fire!

369
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:55,380
Hell's Fire!

370
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:56,260
Hell's Fire!

371
00:17:56,260 --> 00:17:57,060
Hell's Fire!

372
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,040
Hell's Fire!

373
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:00,260
Stand up with the firewrap!

374
00:18:00,340 --> 00:18:01,640
She's a heavenly king.

375
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:04,500
If a single cell remains, she might regenerate.

376
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:06,220
I must obliterate her.

377
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:06,980
Stop it already!

378
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:08,700
You're scaring everyone off!

379
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:09,660
Hell's Fire!

380
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:15,000
Nice.

381
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:17,420
Time to finish it.

382
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:17,600
Huh?

383
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:21,160
Now!

384
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:24,200
Maximum Inferno!

385
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:32,840
Inferno!

386
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:41,440
Hey!

387
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:42,340
Hey!

388
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:43,380
Hell!

389
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:44,000
See, I love myself.

390
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:44,380
I love life.

391
00:18:44,380 --> 00:18:45,220
I love life.

392
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:45,240
It's a big deal.

393
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:50,120
By the power of the Goddess Restartate,

394
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:52,520
may the wounds of this innocent man be healed!

395
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,620
Maximum Inferno!

396
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:57,360
Hey! How long are you gonna do that?

397
00:19:04,260 --> 00:19:05,900
Please, I humbly beg,

398
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:08,740
leave our doubted ones!

399
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:13,140
How did things end up like this?

400
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:15,380
You were more like a demon lord than a hero!

401
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:17,280
One kid threw a rock at me,

402
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:18,980
but I bet you didn't even notice!

403
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:21,060
We saved them from certain doom,

404
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:22,860
and yet they treat us so heartlessly.

405
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:23,460
Lame.

406
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:24,660
You're one to talk, buddy!

407
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:27,280
Poor sweet Jamie didn't burn himself, you know!

408
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:28,100
Not my fault.

409
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:30,540
Oh, wow, you really are the worst.

410
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:31,400
Um...

411
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:33,760
I'm sorry.

412
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:37,220
We shouldn't have made you leave after you rescued everyone.

413
00:19:37,560 --> 00:19:39,300
Oh, no, there's no need to apologize.

414
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:41,380
I mean, your town did burn.

415
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:44,720
Along with a few people, so...

416
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:46,960
It's not much, but here...

417
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:47,560
Ooh, money.

418
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:49,820
You shouldn't be so greedy, Saya!

419
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:51,020
Try to show some restraint!

420
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:51,520
What gives?

421
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:52,920
This isn't very much at all!

422
00:19:53,140 --> 00:19:54,960
If you got any more, then cough it up!

423
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:56,560
You're no better than a thief!

424
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:57,180
Here, sir.

425
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:58,380
It's all I have left.

426
00:19:58,380 --> 00:20:01,640
Hey, mister!

427
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:03,260
You might be a little weird,

428
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:05,520
but deep down inside, you're a real good guy!

429
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:06,900
Oh, Nina.

430
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:10,640
You're sort of right, and sort of wrong.

431
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,160
He's not a good guy.

432
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:13,360
Just super weird.

433
00:20:13,860 --> 00:20:14,140
You...

434
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:15,820
You do realize I'm right here.

435
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:17,620
You burned down their town and robbed them!

436
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,500
I'm being charitable!

437
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:19,860
All right!

438
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:20,980
Let's head off already!

439
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:22,160
Come on, say goodbye!

440
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:24,060
Thank you, Miss Nice Lady!

441
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,380
Thank you too, Mr. Weirdo!

442
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,900
Um, sweetie, let's not address people like that.

443
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:36,460
Listen, don't you think you should start acting a bit more heroic?

444
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:38,360
Oh.

445
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:40,640
Look, you still have that pressed flower.

446
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:43,300
Didn't you say it was a cursed item or something?

447
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,940
Well, that might not be such a bad thing, given our circumstance.

448
00:20:46,940 --> 00:20:50,920
If it attracts enemies, then it might be more convenient for me to hold on to it.

449
00:20:50,980 --> 00:20:51,200
Huh.

450
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:52,220
What?

451
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,420
Oh, it's nothing.

452
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:56,320
Yeesh, I really don't get him.

453
00:20:56,580 --> 00:20:57,560
He's so weird.

454
00:20:58,380 --> 00:20:58,980
Okie doke.

455
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:00,780
Our adventure is just getting started.

456
00:21:01,020 --> 00:21:02,280
Off to the next town!

457
00:21:02,620 --> 00:21:04,400
No, we're going back to the realm.

458
00:21:04,540 --> 00:21:05,260
More training?

459
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:06,300
Are you kidding me?

460
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:09,180
When the enemy learns that we beat a heavenly king,

461
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:11,040
they'll send stronger forces our way.

462
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:13,480
Okay, but if we don't go to the next town,

463
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:15,400
then we won't be able to score any good weapons.

464
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:18,140
Yeah, I would like to buy some new armor, too.

465
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:20,340
Could you make some for me?

466
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:22,140
You can make beds and stuff.

467
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:25,060
I can only create things in the divine realm.

468
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,980
Bringing anything from there is forbidden.

469
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:30,540
And excessive assistance to human is against divine law.

470
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:32,540
So you're useless.

471
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:33,340
Wow!

472
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:35,580
I healed Jamie's burns in case you forgot!

473
00:21:36,180 --> 00:21:37,920
Medicinal herbs could have done the same.

474
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:41,800
In other words, your value to society is no greater than that of a leaf.

475
00:21:42,300 --> 00:21:44,520
Are you comparing me to stuff on a tree?

476
00:21:44,520 --> 00:21:47,060
In any case, I'm due for some more training.

477
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:49,480
Hurry up and open a portal plant, lady.

478
00:21:50,140 --> 00:21:52,000
All right, all right, I hear you.

479
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,720
Wait, why don't you call me?

480
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:55,500
Good.

481
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:56,740
Let's go.

482
00:21:56,980 --> 00:21:58,900
We've just taken a few steps forward,

483
00:21:59,180 --> 00:22:01,940
and then a dozen steps back for the second time.

484
00:22:01,940 --> 00:22:02,120
Yeah!

485
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:06,460
A weirdo hero.

486
00:22:07,060 --> 00:22:08,520
How is this going to work?

487
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:16,060
Well,OK!

488
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:46,040
Thank you.

489
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:49,440
何度目サプライジング

490
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:52,280
やだねどこ行くの

491
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:56,360
ここではぐれたらノーマルーン

492
00:22:56,360 --> 00:23:02,380
離さないであなたへお願いは一個だけ

493
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:06,500
Be perfect please be perfect please

494
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:09,240
未来はきっと繋いだ糸

495
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:13,620
遠く細いけど輝いた絆

496
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:18,020
確かめた追いつけないほらパラサイ

497
00:23:18,020 --> 00:23:20,960
刻んでそっと痛いな一歩

498
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:24,160
愛想のない沖縄の平

499
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:25,440
心配

500
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:27,280
プリズムなの

501
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:29,360
独り

502
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:32,740
愛のために

503
00:23:32,740 --> 00:23:34,060
世界の鍵

504
00:23:34,060 --> 00:23:36,100
本当の勇気は

505
00:23:36,100 --> 00:23:37,600
In your hand

506
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:39,100
抱きしめるよ

